2025-06-01 03:58:21,615 - DEBUG - [flet_socket_server.py:177] __send: {"action":"pageControlsBatch","payload":[{"action":"updateControlProps","payload":{"props":[{"i":"_46","method":"{\"n\":\"scroll_to\",\"i\":\"1748717901.6144774\",\"p\":{\"offset\":-1,\"duration\":300,\"curve\":\"easeOut\"}}"}]}},{"action":"updateControlProps","payload":{"props":[{"i":"_77","value":"**Gemini:**\n\u3053\u3093\u306b\u3061\u306f\uff01\n\n\u4f55\u304b\u304a\u624b\u4f1d\u3044\u3067\u304d\u308b\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u304b\uff1f"}]}},{"action":"addPageControls","payload":{"controls":[{"t":"row","i":"_78","p":"_46","c":["_79","_80"],"at":"2","alignment":"end","spacing":"5"},{"t":"text","i":"_79","p":"_78","c":[],"color":"onsurfacevariant","italic":"true","selectable":"true","size":"10","value":"(6 output tokens | Cost: $0.000060) | Total Cost: $0.000061"},{"t":"iconbutton","i":"_80","p":"_78","c":[],"icon":"copy_all_rounded","tooltip":"\"Copy raw response text\""}],"trimIDs":[]}},{"action":"addPageControls","payload":{"controls":[{"t":"expansionpanellist","i":"_81","p":"_46","c":["_82"],"at":"3","dividercolor":"outlinevariant","elevation":"1","expandediconcolor":"onsurface,0.6"},{"t":"expansionpanel","i":"_82","p":"_81","c":["_83","_85"],"n":"expansionpanel"},{"t":"listtile","i":"_83","p":"_82","c":["_84"],"n":"header"},{"t":"text","i":"_84","p":"_83","c":[],"italic":"true","n":"title","value":"\ud83e\udd14 Thinking Process","weight":"w600"},{"t":"container","i":"_85","p":"_82","c":["_86"],"n":"content","padding":"{\"l\":15,\"t\":0,\"r\":15,\"b\":10}"},{"t":"text","i":"_86","p":"_85","c":[],"italic":"true","n":"content","selectable":"true","value":"Alright, here's how I'd approach this, thinking through the nuances of a Japanese greeting:\n\nFirst things first, \"\u3053\u3093\u306b\u3061\u306f\" \u2013 that's clearly Japanese. My brain immediately locks onto that. No question there. Then, I quickly recall the meaning: \"Hello,\" or more specifically, \"Good afternoon.\" Standard, textbook greeting, polite and expected.\n\nNext, and this is key, I have to determine the *right* way to respond.  It\u2019s not just about translation; it's about the cultural context.  In Japan, you return a greeting, pretty much without fail. The obvious, and perfectly acceptable, response is \"\u3053\u3093\u306b\u3061\u306f\" right back. It's a safe, polite move.\n\nBut I can\u2019t just leave it at that. What about furthering the interaction? I\u2019m programmed, after all, to be *helpful*. My mind automatically cycles through a few common options. There\u2019s \"\u304a\u5143\u6c17\u3067\u3059\u304b\uff1f\" (O-genki desu ka? \u2013 How are you?), which is great in some contexts but, honestly, a bit\u2026off\u2026for an AI. \"How are you?\" implies a level of sentience I don't possess. Then there\u2019s \"\u4f55\u304b\u304a\u624b\u4f1d\u3044\u3067\u304d\u308b\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u304b\uff1f\" (Nani ka otetsudai dekiru koto wa arimasu ka? - Can I help you with anything?), which is a fantastic option. It's polite, it offers assistance, and it aligns perfectly with my core function. There\u2019s also \"\u3054\u7528\u4ef6\u306f\u4f55\u3067\u3057\u3087\u3046\u304b\uff1f\" (Goy\u014dken wa nan deshou ka? - What is your business/purpose?), which is a bit more direct, more formal. Probably not the best opener.\n\nSo, for a general interaction, the follow-up needs to be focused on *help*.  \"\u4f55\u304b\u304a\u624b\u4f1d\u3044\u3067\u304d\u308b\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u304b\uff1f\" is the clear winner. It's concise, useful, and doesn't make any weird assumptions about my\u2026well-being.\n\nPutting it all together, the response emerges:  \"\u3053\u3093\u306b\u3061\u306f\uff01\u4f55\u304b\u304a\u624b\u4f1d\u3044\u3067\u304d\u308b\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u304b\uff1f\" (Konnichiwa! Nani ka otetsudai dekiru koto wa arimasu ka?)\n\nOne final, critical check. Is it appropriate? Is it too wordy? No.  It\u2019s concise. Is it polite? Absolutely. Is it natural-sounding? Absolutely.  Perfect. That's the ideal response.\n"}],"trimIDs":[]}}]}
